\subsection{Innovation-Structured Nonlinear Live ISS}
\label{sec:iss-block-basin}

The nonlinear smallness condition is expressed in the quantities that actually
enter the quaternion geometry.  Velocity and position enter the exact
$v\rightarrow p\rightarrow S$ prediction linearly.  The $S=0$ residual is also
linear; its nonlinear effect occurs only when the full Kalman gain injects part
of that residual into attitude and the quaternion error is reset.

Choose fixed physical scales and let $\vct z=\mat D\vct e_{\rm act}$ be a
dimensionless representation of the active error coordinates of the current
source mode.  Uniform exponential stability from
Theorem~\ref{thm:iss-21-ues} is invariant under this fixed transformation.  Let
$\widetilde\mat A_k^{\rm cl}$ be the corresponding homogeneous normal-Live
transition and write the exact local error recursion as
\begin{equation}
 \vct z_{k+1}
 =\widetilde\mat A_k^{\rm cl}\vct z_k
 +\widetilde\vct\varphi_k(\vct z_k)
 +\widetilde\mat G_k\vct d_k.
 \label{eq:iss-block-recursion}
\end{equation}
In held-bias mode, the frozen accelerometer-bias error is included in
$\vct d_k$.

At a post-prediction, pre-correction sample, the physical residuals have the
local form
\begin{align}
 \vct r_{a,k}
 &=\mat H_{\theta a,k}\delta\vct\theta
   +\mat R_{wb,k}\delta\vct a_w
   +\delta\vct b_a+\vct\epsilon_{a,k},\\
 \vct r_{m,k}
 &=\mat H_{\theta m,k}\delta\vct\theta
   +\vct\epsilon_{m,k},\\
 \vct r_{S,k}&=-\delta\vct S,
 \label{eq:iss-structured-residuals}
\end{align}
with the absent terms deleted when the corresponding measurement or state is
inactive.  On a compact accepted-measurement chart, smoothness of rotation gives
constants for which
\begin{align}
 \|\vct\epsilon_{a,k}\|
 &\le c_{\theta\theta}\|\delta\vct\theta\|^2
     +c_{\theta a}\|\delta\vct\theta\|\,\|\delta\vct a_w\|,\\
 \|\vct\epsilon_{m,k}\|
 &\le c_m\|\delta\vct\theta\|^2.
 \label{eq:iss-residual-remainders}
\end{align}
The attitude component of the complete correction is
\begin{equation}
 \Delta\vct\theta_k
 :=\mat E_\theta\left(
 \mat K_{a,k}\vct r_{a,k}
 +\mat K_{m,k}\vct r_{m,k}
 +\mat K_{S,k}\vct r_{S,k}\right),
 \label{eq:iss-attitude-correction-load}
\end{equation}
where rejected updates contribute zero.  Quaternion injection/reset is smooth
for $\|\Delta\vct\theta_k\|<\Delta_0<\pi$ and its second-order remainder is
bounded by $c_q\|\Delta\vct\theta_k\|^2$.  The nonlinear attitude propagation
adds terms bounded by
$c_{\theta g}\|\delta\vct\theta\|\,\|\delta\vct b_g\|$ and a quadratic
attitude term.

Define the nonlinear geometric load
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal N_k(\vct e):=
 c_1\|\delta\vct\theta\|^2
 +c_2\|\delta\vct\theta\|\,\|\delta\vct b_g\|
 +c_3\|\delta\vct\theta\|\,\|\delta\vct a_w\|
 +c_4\|\Delta\vct\theta_k\|^2.
 \label{eq:iss-nonlinear-load}
\end{equation}

\begin{lemma}[Innovation-structured nonlinear remainder]
\label{lem:iss-block-remainder}
On every compact normal-Live geometry contained in the quaternion chart there
is $c_N<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\widetilde\vct\varphi_k(\vct z)\|
 \le c_N\mathcal N_k(\vct e).}
 \label{eq:iss-block-remainder}
\end{equation}
There is no direct term proportional to
$\|\delta v\|^2$, $\|\delta p\|^2$, $\|\delta S\|^2$,
$\|\delta a_w\|^2$, or $\|\delta b_a\|^2$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
The exact additive prediction is affine in $(v,p,S,a_w,b_a)$ for fixed
attitude and source parameters.  The physical accelerometer and magnetometer
maps are smooth rotations; Taylor expansion gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:iss-residual-remainders}.  The integral residual is exactly
linear.  Additive-state injection is exact.  The only nonlinear effect of a
large linear residual on the attitude coordinates is therefore through the
actual gain-weighted correction of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:iss-attitude-correction-load}, followed by quaternion
injection/reset.  Smoothness of that map on
$\|\Delta\theta\|<\Delta_0$ gives the stated quadratic correction term.  The
attitude prediction supplies the remaining attitude/gyro-bias products.  All
first-order terms belong to $\widetilde A_k^{\rm cl}$, which proves the bound.
\end{proof}

The bound permits a comparatively large $S$ or accelerometer-bias error when
its attitude cross-gain is small enough that
$\|\Delta\vct\theta_k\|$ remains inside the geometric tube.  Likewise a large
latent-acceleration error is compatible with the local geometry when the
product with the attitude error remains small.

\subsubsection{Time-varying Lyapunov metric}

UES of the active homogeneous transition implies the existence of a bounded
quadratic Lyapunov sequence.  For any fixed $\mat Q\succ0$, define
\begin{equation}
 \mat P_k:=\sum_{j=k}^{\infty}
 \widetilde\Psi(j,k)^\top\mat Q\widetilde\Psi(j,k).
 \label{eq:iss-converse-P}
\end{equation}
The series converges uniformly, and constants
$0<p_-\le p_+<\infty$ and $q_->0$ exist such that
\begin{align}
 p_-\mat I&\preceq\mat P_k\preceq p_+\mat I,\\
 \widetilde A_k^{{\rm cl}\top}\mat P_{k+1}
 \widetilde A_k^{\rm cl}-\mat P_k
 &\preceq-q_-\mat I.
 \label{eq:iss-converse-decrease}
\end{align}
Let $V_k(\vct z)=\vct z^\top\mat P_k\vct z$.

For a compact structured tube $\mathcal T_k$ inside the accepted quaternion and
measurement geometry, define
\begin{equation}
 \ell_{\mathcal T}:=
 \sup_k\sup_{\substack{\vct z\in\mathcal T_k\\\vct z\ne0}}
 \frac{c_N\mathcal N_k(\vct e)}{\|\vct z\|}.
 \label{eq:iss-structured-lipschitz}
\end{equation}
This quantity depends on the actual attitude error, attitude--bias and
attitude--$a_w$ products, and gain-weighted attitude correction, rather than on
a common radius for every state coordinate.

\begin{theorem}[Innovation-structured local practical ISS]
\label{thm:iss-block-local}
Assume the applicable mode of Theorem~\ref{thm:iss-21-ues},
Lemma~\ref{lem:iss-block-remainder}, and
$\|\widetilde G_k\|\le\bar G$.  Let
$\bar A:=\sup_k\|\widetilde A_k^{\rm cl}\|$.  If a compact tube
$\mathcal T_k$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 2p_+\bar A\ell_{\mathcal T}
 +p_+\ell_{\mathcal T}^2
 <\frac{q_-}{2},}
 \label{eq:iss-block-basin}
\end{equation}
then every sufficiently small Lyapunov sublevel
$\Omega_{c,k}:=\{\vct z:V_k(\vct z)\le c\}$ contained in
$\mathcal T_k$ is robustly invariant for a sufficiently small bounded input.
On that sublevel there exist $0<\lambda_z<1$ and $\Gamma_z<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_k^{1/2}
 \le \lambda_z^{k-j}V_j^{1/2}
 +\Gamma_z\|\vct d\|_{\infty,[j,k)}.}
 \label{eq:iss-block-local-bound}
\end{equation}
The statement applies to the active 18-state held-bias coordinates with the
held bias in $\vct d$, to the active 21-state mode after bias release, and after
projection to the gravity-only yaw quotient.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
For zero input, substitute Eq.~\eqref{eq:iss-block-recursion} in
$V_{k+1}-V_k$ and use Eq.~\eqref{eq:iss-converse-decrease}.  On
$\mathcal T_k$,
$\|\widetilde\varphi_k\|\le\ell_{\mathcal T}\|z_k\|$, so the two cross terms
are bounded by
$2p_+\bar A\ell_{\mathcal T}\|z_k\|^2$ and the quadratic remainder term by
$p_+\ell_{\mathcal T}^2\|z_k\|^2$.  Equation~\eqref{eq:iss-block-basin}
therefore leaves a strict negative margin.  The bounded-input terms are handled
with Young inequalities, giving
\begin{equation}
 V_{k+1}\le(1-\alpha_z)V_k+c_d\|d_k\|^2
\end{equation}
for some $\alpha_z>0$.  Choose $c$ and the input bound so that the right-hand
side points inward on the boundary of $\Omega_{c,k}$; induction gives robust
invariance.  Iteration and norm equivalence give
Eq.~\eqref{eq:iss-block-local-bound}.
\end{proof}

For certificate construction, $\mathcal T_k$ is chosen from physically
meaningful bounds on tilt, the gain-weighted correction angle, and the mixed
attitude products.  The regional map of Sec.~\ref{sec:finite-live-capture}
verifies finite entry into a sublevel satisfying
Eq.~\eqref{eq:iss-block-basin}.
